🎬 Movie Genre Classification using Machine Learning ✅

Excited to share that I’ve successfully completed a machine learning project that predicts the genre of a movie based on its plot summary using NLP techniques! 🧠📚

🔧 Tech Stack & Methods Used:

TF-IDF for feature extraction

Logistic Regression, Naive Bayes, and SVM for classification

Scikit-learn for model building and evaluation

Hands-on with data preprocessing, model tuning, and evaluation using accuracy and classification reports

This project was a great opportunity to explore text classification and understand how machine learning can interpret and classify human language effectively.

💡 It’s fascinating how a few lines of plot can tell a model so much about genre—action, romance, fantasy, or sci-fi!

Looking forward to applying these skills to more real-world NLP problems.

